Item 7 first tranche: reports layer, its tests, and a combo bug it found

Five core reports plus the infrastructure the deferred seven will inherit:
purchase & sell, stock, profit & loss, tax, and expenses, behind a
permission-filtered hub.

ReportService owns every figure and the controller owns none. The reason is
scoped(): "this month, at the locations you may see" appeared four times in
HomeController::totals() alone, and four copies of that phrase are four chances
for the dashboard and the report to quietly disagree. HomeController::dateRange()
now delegates rather than holding a second current-month default.

Two figure decisions, both recorded in NOTES 13.2 because they are decisions:
COGS uses purchase_price_inc_tax, matching what StockService::consume() already
writes into the FIFO map -- computing it from the exclusive column would make the
same sale show two different profits depending on which screen you opened. And
quantities are net of returns on both sides, so a returned item stops counting as
both revenue and cost.

export() is one action parameterised by report name and whitelist-validated,
rather than five near-identical methods: one gate, one Excel::download, and a
parameter that reaches a method name is never trusted.

ReportsTest (17 tests) asserts the arithmetic rather than the rendering, and
found a production bug in selling, not in reporting: SellService::syncLines()
collected only parent line ids into keptIds, so its "delete everything not kept"
sweep destroyed the combo component lines consumeComboComponents() had just
written and released the stock it had just consumed -- on every combo sale, not
only on edits. Nothing looked wrong on screen; the FIFO map was simply empty, so
every combo reported as pure margin at zero cost on the one report an owner makes
decisions with. Fixed by threading the child ids back, which stays correct on the
edit path because the previous save's children are still absent from keptIds.

Those tests also reported a confident 0.0 for thirteen figures until setUp()
signed a user in: permittedLocations() resolves against auth()->user(), and
createTenant() authenticates nobody, so every assertion was passing against an
empty report. Both halves of the COGS join were then mutation-checked per 12.4.

ApiResponseTest (14 tests) closes 12.5. Thirteen endpoints sitting in
ScreensRenderTest::SKIP had no test at all, and they are the POS product search,
every contact picker and the purchase-form prefill. It asserts what a render walk
structurally cannot: a JSON content type rather than a redirect, the field names
the front end binds to, and the failure modes -- including the four cases that
pin Product::scopeForLocation(), whose last regression was a hard SQL error that
nothing could see.

No new CSS: .tile, .rise-group, x-stat and .filter-bar already carry the design
directive, and .filter-bar is already in the print hide list.

php artisan test -- 102 tests, 494 assertions, all passing.
Lang parity ar=974 en=974, +68 each, every new key present once in both.

Seven reports remain deferred and are named explicitly in 10.2 so this tranche
is not mistaken for the finished item.

